{code,core,types,ui}: split long functions instead of allowing too_many_lines

The codebase had accumulated several functions that exceeded the
clippy::too_many_lines default and were each silenced with a local
`#[allow]`. That makes the lint toothless and hides where real
refactoring is needed.

This commit extracts helpers without changing behavior:
 - lofi-code::run_code_mode splits its preamble, host-async driver,
   cleanup, and loop-slice trimmer into named helpers; the entry fn
   drops from ~195 lines to a short orchestration
 - BuiltinTools::bind_tools splits schema construction
   (jobs_tool_schema, bind_tools_inner) from the registration loop
 - BashTool::exec splits command validation, sandbox policy wiring,
   and the spawn driver into helpers
 - openai_completions::map_openai_history extracts
   sanitize_message_content, push_orphaned_tool_output_tail,
   sink_dangling_tool_carryover, and the assistant/tool/user/system
   mappers
 - lofi-ui::tests::initial_app splits PTY echo stub and CWD-lock
   warm-up from the app constructor

agent_run's format_dangling_appendix picks up the small final carry
formatting helper so its callers stay short.